"comparison": "Both companies disclose their adoption of Extreme Ultraviolet (EUV) lithography for leading-edge process nodes in 2024, but differ in specific node nomenclature and manufacturing scope. Micron (MU) identifies its '1γ' node as the first to employ EUV lithography for DRAM volume shipments expected in 2025, having transitioned production in 2024 to 1α and 1β nodes. In contrast, Intel (INTC) identifies 'Intel 4' and 'Intel 3' as its first EUV lithography nodes, which moved to high-volume manufacturing in 2024 for processor production, specifically noting Intel 4 is expected to represent an increasing portion of production in 2025. While both leverage EUV for advanced nodes in the same timeframe, MU focuses on DRAM memory nodes (1γ) while INTC focuses on CPU logic nodes (Intel 4/3).",
